WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:14.689
At school we speak English.

2
00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:19.088
But we speak many other languages too.

3
00:00:19.089 --> 00:00:22.470
Mrs. Berman is from Germany.

4
00:00:22.471 --> 00:00:26.397
"Good morning, class," she says.

5
00:00:26.398 --> 00:00:33.182
"Good morning," we say in German. "Guten Morgen!"

6
00:00:33.183 --> 00:00:36.848
Koji's grandfather is from Japan.

7
00:00:36.849 --> 00:00:39.445
He visits our classroom.

8
00:00:39.446 --> 00:00:45.364
We say "welcome" in Japanese. "Yōkoso."

9
00:00:45.365 --> 00:00:48.381
Mr. Como is from Italy.

10
00:00:48.382 --> 00:00:51.321
He is our music teacher.

11
00:00:51.322 --> 00:00:57.117
We sing "hello" in Italian. "Ciao!"

12
00:00:57.118 --> 00:00:59.892
David is from China.

13
00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:02.719
He brings dumplings from home.

14
00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:08.628
We say "thank you" in Chinese. "Xie-xie."

15
00:01:08.629 --> 00:01:11.708
Jane's friend lives in France.

16
00:01:11.709 --> 00:01:14.854
Jane teaches us words in French.

17
00:01:14.855 --> 00:01:19.699
Au revoir means "good-bye."

18
00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:22.871
Miss Isabel is from Spain.

19
00:01:22.872 --> 00:01:28.287
She makes hot soup for lunch.

20
00:01:28.288 --> 00:01:34.309
"Yum!" we say in Spanish. "Es rico!"

21
00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:37.274
Hana is from Korea.

22
00:01:37.275 --> 00:01:41.957
She shows us how to write in Korean.

23
00:01:41.958 --> 00:01:48.841
I write "mom." "Umma."

24
00:01:48.842 --> 00:01:51.844
I can speak many languages.

25
00:01:51.845 --> 00:01:57.329
What languages can you speak?
